   207	
   208	**Why the existing models do not cover the pair.** Every S-P3 model signs every slot with the library's single
   209	family `sign/checksign`, which carries one DSKS capability. The mixed pair has two schemes, chosen per slot by one
   210	id. That is a different signature algebra, so "passes P3's model" needs a model run. Reading the old green results
   211	across would not do.
   212	
   213	**The model change** (`formal/suite/s-p3/proverif/hybrid/`, derived from Q5 recut 3 and nothing else changed):
   214	- slot A (= kms) signs possession and attestation with a second, model-local family `signR/checksignR`;
   215	- that family has **its own DSKS capability** `dsksR`, of the library's shape. This is conservative: ML-DSA is not
   216	  assumed to resist key substitution;
   217	- slot B (= gpg) keeps the library family;
   218	- both frames and the tuple carry one value `algPair`;
   219	- the verifier accepts only `algPair`, and checks slot A with `checksignR` and slot B with `checksign`, for both the
   220	  possession proof and the attestation.
   221	
   222	Predictions were written into each model header before the first run of any of them.
   223	
   224	| Model | Prediction (pre-run) | Observed | Outcome |
   225	|---|---|---|---|
   226	| H1 correct (`sp3_h1_hybrid_correct.pv`) | ReattributedA, ReattributedB, PossessionTransplanted unreachable; N1 reachable (p~0.85) | all three **unreachable**; HonestAccepted and Accept2 **reachable** | **as predicted** |
   227	| H2 broken: slot A possession unnamed (`sp3_h2_companion_possession_unnamed_R.pv`) | PossessionTransplanted reachable through `dsksR` (p~0.75) | PossessionTransplanted **reachable**; the derivation applies `dsksR` to the honest rule-R possession signature of `skA2`; Reattributed A/B unreachable | **red as predicted**: the rule-R family's DSKS capability is live in H1 |
   228	| H3 broken: slot A frame unbound (`sp3_h3_companion_unboundA_R.pv`) | ReattributedA reachable only (p~0.75) | ReattributedA **reachable**; ReattributedB and PossessionTransplanted unreachable | **red on exactly slot A** |
   229	| H4 rule O applied to both slots (`sp3_h4_companion_single_rule.pv`) | HonestAccepted unreachable; Accept2 reachable (p~0.8) | HonestAccepted **unreachable**; Accept2 reachable; no violation reachable | **as predicted**: wrong rule selection fails closed (liveness), not open |
   230	
   231	Run (ProVerif 2.05, about one second per model, against boxes of 15–30 minutes):
