   261	| `KMS-MLDSA65-PURE-GPG-OPENPGP4-ECDSA-P256-SHA256` (hybrid pair id; registered by the branch-registration supplement of <DATE>, A9.6) | rule R: ML-DSA-65 (FIPS 204), pure, empty context | rule O (OpenPGP P-256; slot-2 custody per A9.6) | `kms`: exactly 3309; `gpg`: 1024 |
   262	```
   263	
   264	**Rule R block (replaces the five bullets from "The signed message is the frame itself." to "They are added when an
   265	id is registered."):**
   266	
   267	```
   268	- The signed message is the frame itself (`F_manifest` for a possession proof). No trailer, no transformation.
   269	- **Registered pair (branch-registration supplement of <DATE>, A9.6).** `KMS-MLDSA65-PURE-GPG-OPENPGP4-ECDSA-P256-SHA256`:
   270	  slot `kms` is ML-DSA-65 (FIPS 204) in pure mode with the empty context, so the FIPS 204 message representative is
   271	  `0x00 ‖ 0x00 ‖ F`; slot `gpg` is rule O. `S_kms` is exactly 3309 bytes. Length 0 gives `SIG_EMPTY`, above 3309
   272	  `LENGTH_CAP`, any other length `SIG_FORMAT`. The codec reads no byte of `S_kms`: a malformed hint encoding or an
   273	  out-of-range `z` is a verification failure (`SIG_INVALID`; `POSSESSION_INVALID` for possession), not a codec code.
   274	- The issuer obtains `S_kms` (attestation and possession) from KMS with `MessageType EXTERNAL_MU` only, sending
   275	  μ = SHAKE256(SHAKE256(pk, 64) ‖ 0x00 ‖ 0x00 ‖ F, 64), pk the raw 1952-byte key (RFC 9881 Appendix D). The result is
   276	  an ordinary pure signature over `F`. The verifier never sees μ and verifies over `F`.
