    58	## A5.1 P9's conformance vector: what it must carry — ADOPTED (author)
    59	
    60	**What Amendment 4 says.** §A4.1(ii): one H1a red-bar vector — the
    61	same bundle and declared policy, verified on two isolated machines
    62	with no network, must yield the same verdict, and a verifier that
    63	consults any optional service must fail the vector.
    64	
    65	**What the P9 probe showed** (`formal/spike/tla-probes/P9/RESULTS-PROBE.md`
    66	F2–F4; three stateful verifiers written besides the pure one —
    67	`LIVE_FALLBACK`, `LIVE_FAILCLOSED`, `REPLAY_LATCH`. On the two-machine
    68	VECTOR configuration two of the three are wholly undetected
    69	(`LiveFallback_Vector.out`, `ReplayLatch_Vector.out`: both invariants
    70	green) and the third is caught only by the probe's `Purity`
    71	invariant — the expected-verdict oracle that §A4.1(ii) as worded does
    72	not carry; its agreement clause, which is what the wording says,
    73	passes all three). (a) A verifier that consults an optional service and falls
    74	back to the bundle when the service is unreachable is
    75	indistinguishable from a pure one on two isolated machines. (b) A
    76	fail-closed consulting verifier returns `UNVERIFIABLE` on both
    77	machines: they agree with each other and disagree with what bundle
    78	plus policy determine. (c) Verifier-local history (a replay latch) is
    79	invisible to two fresh machines.
    80	
    81	**§A4.1(ii) is hereby written as:** the vector carries the **expected
    82	verdict** determined by bundle and declared policy; each machine's
    83	verdict is compared to *that*, not only to the other machine's; one
    84	case presents the same bundle twice on one machine and requires the
    85	same verdict both times; and the clause "a verifier that consults any
    86	optional service must fail" is discharged by the inspection leg (i)
    87	together with one case in which the optional service is reachable and
    88	contradicts the bundle, not by the two-machine run alone. P9's
    89	discharge label is unchanged: **[inspection + vector]**. This is a
    90	precision repair in the A4.2 style: the obligation is made to catch
    91	what its own probe showed it missed; nothing is weakened.
