   202	## A5.6 Standing binds to the identity in the core, not only to the key — ADOPTED (author)
   203	
   204	The review (item 23) showed a core issued under identity A, with its
   205	honest terminal lineage record, gains standing under a second honest
   206	authority tuple naming the same key as identity B, because the
   207	standing path binds the key to the presented tuple and never the
   208	presented tuple to the core's embedded one. Registered: the standing
   209	path checks that the presented authority tuple equals the tuple
   210	embedded in the core it derives the artifact identity from —
   211	`ENUMERATION.md` note 4 item 2's principle (the standing path relies
   212	on nothing the envelope path established), applied to the tuple as it
   213	is already applied to the key; an alias companion must go red. What
   214	this does **not** decide: whether an issuer holding two identities on
   215	one key keeps one terminal lineage record or two. The check settles
   216	only that a core issued under one identity cannot gain standing when
   217	presented under the other; a single TLR under that key may still name
   218	cores from both. Registered in `formal/suite/s-standing/PREDICTIONS.md` as a
   219	post-freeze addendum.
